add(3,"who sees a skull sticking out of the clay, with one great eye.","bakedX","none (prop)","firelit edge","push-in","X:NB19","Tight crop; the central opening reads as an eye. Needs a clean NB19 skull, else use DG-01")
add(3,"Everything else, he wrote, was added later. It is imagination, not evidence.","bakedX","anonymous sailor (back view)","cold daylight beach cave","hold","X:NB20 + CODE:overlay-abel","Lower-third paraphrase: 'Abel, 1914: a plausible picture, offered without evidence'")
add(3,"The idea found a champion in Adrienne Mayor, a Stanford folklorist and historian of science.","card","none","flat parchment, cool","hold","CODE:card-mayor","Name, book, 2000. Typography only; no cover art, no portrait",True)
add(3,"In The First Fossil Hunters, she argues that Greeks and Romans noticed big fossil bones,","baked","two small visitors (extras)","overcast daylight, stone porch","push-in","NB21","Sanctuary porch, giant bone on a plinth, two tiny visitors. DRIFT: new faces; keep them tiny")
add(3,"collected them, measured them, and tried to explain them.","bakedX","none","overcast daylight","hold","X:NB21 + CODE:measuring-rod","Crop on the bone, rod overlay")
add(3,"Giants, and one-eyed monsters, may owe something to those finds.","bakedX","none","overcast daylight","push-in","X:NB21 + CODE:overlay-may","Different crop; the word 'may' picked out")
add(3,"On the Cyclops, though, Mayor herself is careful.","card","none","flat parchment ledger","hold","CODE:ledger-mayor-careful","Row: 'Mayor on the Cyclops: careful'")
