# ---------------- ch4: what we can and cannot say ----------------
add(5,"So where does that leave us? Start with what is solid.","card","none","flat parchment ledger","hold","CODE:ledger-solid-not","Two columns: SOLID / NOT SOLID",True)
add(5,"The Greeks told at least three different Cyclops stories, and kept them apart.","diagram","Cyclops cy_v4 (existing crops)","dark ledger","hold","CODE:three-columns (RC02 / NB22 / NBG07)","Shepherd / smith / wall-builders")
add(5,"A single eye is stated by Hesiod, Euripides, and Theocritus. Homer implies it.","card","none","flat parchment ledger","hold","CODE:ledger-attested","Three ticked rows; Homer row marked 'implied'")
add(5,"Dwarf elephants really lived on those islands, and their skulls really do have a hole in the middle.","diagram","none","white, archival","hold","CODE:skull-front (DG-01)","Skull plate with island dots inset")
add(5,"The blinding story itself is a folktale. Scholars have counted over two hundred versions,","map","none","flat parchment","push-in","CODE:map-world-folktale","Regional markers only (Iceland, Britain/Ireland, Portugal, Africa, Turkey, Russia, Arabia, Korea)")
add(5,"from Iceland to Korea, and most think the tale is older than Homer.","map","none","flat parchment","hold","CODE:map-world-folktale","Counter '200+ versions'")
add(5,"That does not rule out the skull. It does mean the story does not need one.","bakedX","Odysseus","fire-lit close-up","push-in","X:RS07","Second use of slot 07 (crop)")
add(5,"Now, what we cannot say. No surviving ancient text says anyone mistook a skull for a Cyclops.","bakedX","none (prop)","firelit edge","hold","X:NB19 + CODE:overlay-not-stated","Lower-third: 'ancient source: none found'")
add(5,"Other explanations compete: volcanic craters, smith guilds, even a birth defect called cyclopia,","bakedX","none","night crater glow","hold","X:NBG06","Crater crop")
add(5,"though in that condition the eye sits below the nose, not above it.","card","none","flat parchment ledger","hold","CODE:card-cyclopia","Text only; no medical imagery")
add(5,"Aguirre and Buxton's verdict is that each has an air of plausibility, and none has proof.","card","none","flat parchment ledger","hold","CODE:ledger-verdict","Four candidates, PROOF column blank")
add(5,"The skull theory is a hypothesis. A plausible one, and still unproven.","diagram","none","white, archival","hold","CODE:skull-front (DG-01) + stamp","Stamp HYPOTHESIS, restrained")
# ---------------- verdict ----------------
